A||N||3||BlackARROW||Fan prob.  Need help about location.||||12||
Z||000000||BlackARROW||05-02-2001||08:32 PM||||And it was a damn warm day.   <P>I was wishing my rad fan would start working on again. <P>I have the Haynes book about the Fiero, but they don't show the location of the temp switch and all that.  I have to locate the coolant temp switch (and wire) and the fan relay.  Too bad the wires just look black and black.   <P>I've tested the connection near the thermostat housing. I got a bright light on one, and a dimmed light on the other one.  I'm confused. Is it the good one?  <P>Thanks in advance<P>BA-&gt;<BR>Fiero 2M4 '85<P>||||reg||12
Z||000001||johnt671||05-02-2001||09:51 PM||||If you have a 4 cyl the temp switch is on the drivers side  near the end of the the exaust manifold.  If you start at the thermostat housing look over to the right and down near the manifold.  You may may need to move some wires around to see it. It should have a green and white wire going to it, or if it looks like mine did, no wire and a melted blob of plastic on top.||||reg||1
Z||000002||BlackARROW||05-03-2001||12:59 AM||||Thanks John.  You've helped me fixed my problem.<P><BR>I found that connector, exactly where you told me.  Only one exception - it was hanging behind.  The plastic probably melted as you said.  Well now I've grounded it, so as soon as I start the engine, the fan goes on.  I got no problem with that.<P><BR>Now I'm working on a homemade squarry scoop for the air entry on the side.  So far, I did a test with a cardboard that I've mold by hand (but painted it with the exact color of the car, and even putting some clearcoat on, so it won't show too much).  Tomorrow I will be testing it's efficiency, if it works well, I'll take the model to create a real one, out of plastic or aluminium.  I've looked at it, and it gives a great look<P><BR>Stay sharp<P><BR>BA-&gt;<BR>Fiero 2M4 '85<P><BR><p>[This message has been edited by BlackARROW (edited 05-03-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||johnt671||05-03-2001||02:30 PM||||Glad you found it, it took me about two hrs to find mine(off and on hunting).  I bought a lower temp one from Rodney Dickman but I still haven" been able to find the wire for it.  It was cut and spliced somewhere inside the harness, so I gave up and put in a toggle switch instead.||||reg||1
